From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:59:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 094/148] hjviewer: ask the access password before connecting
 (A0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

UX-G1 (U11, decided A0): on a server known to be staff-only (enforce,
closed), an app without a login that keeps no access password ticket
for the PC gets A0 from connect() before any session opens: A1's
content as A0's words, for cards, the ID field and Connect's items
alike. [연결] trades the access password for that PC's ticket and then
opens the session, [로그인] opens it after the login, [취소] opens
nothing. The desktop opens the field at once; a phone keeps it behind
"이용 비밀번호가 있나요?" as A1 does. Enter connects with something
typed, else logs in. An unknown mode, a session window's new
connection and a desktop link open the session as before, and a
refusal brings A1.

The core answers main_get_common("hjv-guest-held:<PC ID>") with "Y"
while this process keeps a ticket for that PC that holds, never the
ticket; the PC password box shows A1's note once per session then,
also in a desktop session window, which cannot see the main window's
memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
